commitResults.messageBody:
* Parser input must be non-null;
--* Dobby calls it only after a successful console read.
* Numbered-command flags cannot represent both mark and delete;
--* that combination indicates incorrect parser wiring.
* Marker searches require non-null tokens/markers and a valid start index;
--* because these are private helper contracts.
* Token joining requires a valid array range;
--* violating it indicates a parser implementation error.
* Tasks require non-blank descriptions;
--* because user and saved-data validation should reject missing descriptions beforehand.
* Saved task lines must be non-null;
--* because the storage reader produces real strings.
* Task lists and saved collections cannot contain null tasks;
--* because display and persistence operations assume valid Task objects.
* Loaded-task counts cannot be negative, and loaded collection must exist;
--* because these are result-state invariants.
* Date parsing requires non-null text;
--* because callers provide parsed command or stored-record text.
* A parsed date/time must have a value;
--* date-only values must use midnight so hasTime remains consistent with the stored value.
